    {
      "id": "msg-2",
      "role": "assistant",
      "text": "I've built the L bracket. It's molded ABS, 4 mm thick and 20 mm wide, with two 40 mm legs. Each leg has an M4 clearance hole (Ø4.5 mm), 24 mm from the outside corner and centred across the width.\n\n- **Checks:** the wall thickness (at least 2 mm), draft (at least 1°) and material checks pass, and the report lists no risks.\n- **Draft:** I assumed the mould opens along the 20 mm width. The walls taper 1.5° in that direction, and the legs stay at least 2 mm thick even at the thin end.\n- **Not tested:** no check covers strength, drop or heat, so those need review by hand.\n\nYou can change the leg lengths, thickness, width, hole size and hole positions as parameters.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-18T10:42:23.871254Z",
